/// <summary>
/// Structured failure envelope an <c>agentTool()</c> returns when a sub-agent run
/// does not complete. Instead of an opaque error string the parent model would
/// parrot back to the user, the caller (or an orchestration harness) gets a
/// machine-readable signal:
/// <br /><br />
/// - <c>status</c> mirrors the underlying terminal status (<c>error</c> | <c>aborted</c> |
///   <c>interrupted</c>).
/// - <c>retryable</c> is <c>true</c> only for a transient interruption — the child was
///   reset or superseded by a deploy / parent recovery and never reached a
